    "swagger": "2.0",
    "info": {
        "description": "A comprehensive Go web application template using the Fiber framework with essential features including API documentation, database management, structured response handling, clean architecture patterns, and secure authentication.\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start Guide\n\n### 1. Authentication Flow\nThis API uses JWT (JSON Web Token) for authentication. Follow these steps to get started:\n\n**Step 1: Register or Login**\n- **Register**: Use `POST /auth/register` to create a new account\n- **Login**: Use `POST /auth/login` with existing credentials\n\n**Step 2: Authorize in Swagger**\n1. Copy the `access_token` from the login/register response\n2. Click the **\"Authorize\"** button at the top of this page\n3. Enter: `Bearer {your-access-token}` (replace with your actual token)\n4. Click **\"Authorize\"** to save the token\n\n**Step 3: Test Protected Endpoints**\n- All User Management endpoints now include your authorization automatically\n- Try the `GET /users` endpoint to list users\n\n**Step 4: Token Management**\n- **Access tokens expire in 15 minutes** - use `POST /auth/refresh` to get new tokens\n- **Logout** using `POST /auth/logout` to invalidate tokens when done\n\n### 2. Example Authentication Flow\n```\n1. POST /auth/register → Get access_token and refresh_token\n2. Click \"Authorize\" → Enter \"Bearer {access_token}\"\n3. Test protected endpoints (GET /users, PUT /users/{id}, etc.)\n4. When token expires → POST /auth/refresh with refresh_token\n5. POST /auth/logout → Clean logout and token invalidation\n```\n\n## 📋 API Response Format\nAll API responses follow a consistent structure for predictable client integration:\n\n**Success Response:**\n```json\n{\n\"success\": true,\n\"message\": \"Operation successful\",\n\"data\": { ... },\n\"error\": null,\n\"meta\": { ... }\n}\n```\n\n**Error Response:**\n```json\n{\n\"success\": false,\n\"message\": \"Request failed\",\n\"data\": null,\n\"error\": {\n\"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n\"message\": \"Validation failed\",\n\"details\": { \"email\": \"Email is required\" }\n},\n\"meta\": null\n}\n```\n\n## ⚠️ Error Handling\nThe API uses standard HTTP status codes and provides detailed error information:\n\n**Common Error Codes:**\n- `VALIDATION_ERROR` (400): Request validation failed\n- `UNAUTHORIZED` (401): Invalid credentials or expired token\n- `FORBIDDEN` (403): Access denied\n- `NOT_FOUND` (404): Resource not found\n- `CONFLICT` (409): Resource already exists (e.g., email already registered)\n- `INTERNAL_ERROR` (500): Server error\n\n**Error Response Fields:**\n- `success`: Always `false` for errors\n- `message`: Always \"Request failed\" for errors\n- `error.code`: Specific error code for programmatic handling\n- `error.message`: Human-readable error message\n- `error.details`: Field-specific validation errors (when applicable)\n\n## 📄 Pagination\nList endpoints support pagination with consistent query parameters:\n\n**Query Parameters:**\n- `page`: Page number (default: 1, minimum: 1)\n- `limit`: Items per page (default: 10, minimum: 1, maximum: 100)\n\n**Pagination Response:**\n```json\n{\n\"success\": true,\n\"message\": \"Users retrieved successfully\",\n\"data\": [ ... ],\n\"meta\": {\n\"page\": 1,\n\"limit\": 10,\n\"total\": 100,\n\"total_pages\": 10\n}\n}\n```\n\n## 🔍 Search and Filtering\nUser endpoints support advanced search and filtering:\n\n**Search Parameters:**\n- `search`: Search in first_name, last_name, and email fields\n- `is_active`: Filter by user active status (true/false)\n- `sort_by`: Sort field (id, email, first_name, last_name, is_active, created_at, updated_at)\n- `sort_order`: Sort direction (asc, desc)\n\n**Example:** `GET /users?search=john\u0026is_active=true\u0026sort_by=created_at\u0026sort_order=desc`\n\n## 🔐 Security Features\n- **JWT Authentication**: Secure token-based authentication\n- **Password Hashing**: Bcrypt encryption for user passwords\n- **Token Blacklisting**: Secure logout with token invalidation\n- **Input Validation**: Comprehensive request validation\n- **Rate Limiting**: API rate limiting to prevent abuse\n- **CORS Support**: Configurable cross-origin resource sharing",
        "title": "Go Fiber Template API",
